  "result": "Perfect! All 79 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n**New file `src/numbering.js`:**\n- **`nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)`** \u2014 Generates the next invoice number\n  - Returns format: `INV-<year>-<counter>` (e.g., `INV-2025-0042`)\n  - Counter is 4-digit zero-padded (0001, 0002, ..., 9999)\n  - Counter resets to 0001 for each new year\n  - Ignores malformed numbers and numbers from other years\n  - Correctly handles unordered input arrays\n\n**New function in `src/invoices.js`:**\n- **`issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)`** \u2014 Issue an invoice\n  - Assigns the next invoice number using `nextInvoiceNumber()`\n  - Changes status from 'draft' to 'issued'\n  - Adds `number` field to the returned invoice\n  - Returns `NOT_DRAFT` if invoice status isn't 'draft'\n  - Never mutates the input invoice\n\n**Added 18 new tests:**\n- **10 tests for `nextInvoiceNumber`** covering:\n  - First invoice of year\n  - Counter incrementing and unordered arrays\n  - Year-by-year counter resets\n  - Mixed years and high counters\n  - Malformed number handling\n  \n- **8 tests for `issueInvoice`** covering:\n  - Number assignment and status change\n  - Data preservation\n  - Using existing numbers for next counter\n  - Different years independence\n  - NOT_DRAFT error handling\n  - Immutability preservation\n  - Chaining with `addLine()`\n\nAll invoice numbers follow the format `INV-YYYY-NNNN` with independent counters per year. \u2713",
